Scope: kept as one commit. The expiry pitfall could read as an unrelated
"while in the area" addition, but it's the necessary bound on the "an empty
cache is normal" reassurance this same commit adds to Step 1 — without it,
that advice masks the one case (gc pruning between passes) where an empty
cache is a genuine problem. One qualifies the other, so they land together.

Includes a 0.1.14 patch bump (docs/clarification, no behavioral change).

The gc figures (60 days resolved / 15 unresolved) are git's documented
defaults for gc.rerereResolved / gc.rerereUnresolved; I did not inspect the
user's local config, hence the "by default" phrasing in the pitfall text.
